Parent: #1
Foundation branch: `foundation/domain-decoupled-core-v0`
Current remote base subject before this work: `0008d99873f815b23f0bea0c9fca989a20b0637e`.

## Goal
Publish the minimal executable repository foundation that every later workstream can consume without re-deriving architecture: root policy/SSOT, deterministic reference primitives, CI, evidence/public-boundary hooks, State Machine/DAG/data-flow documentation, worker prompt/task packet, and handoff contract.

## Owns for this atom
- root `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `.gitignore`, `LICENSE`, `NOTICE`, `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `Makefile`, `pyproject.toml`;
- `.github/workflows/validate.yml`;
- `src/edge_tlm/**` deterministic Foundation primitives only;
- `tests/**` Foundation tests and self-contained fixtures only;
- `docs/architecture/**`;
- generic `docs/agents/**` prompt/handoff/task-packet surfaces;
- selected Foundation governance docs: evidence policy, technology selection, Stack/readiness/publication manifest, Shadow checkpoint, Local Handoff method.

## Explicit exclusions
- `docs/research/**` -> #2;
- public/private resolver implementation and P1-owned boundary document -> #7;
- `contracts/**` and generated bindings -> #3;
- native adapters -> #4/#5/#6/#8;
- `models/**` -> #9;
- `skills/**` -> #10;
- production `core/**` -> #11;
- `training/**`, `eval/**` -> #12;
- `apps/**` -> #13;
- private Google Workspace URLs/values, product roadmap/commercial text, model weights, private datasets, credentials/secrets -> never public.

## Exact task contract
The local candidate contains `docs/agents/packets/foundation-15.task.json`, bound to base/rollback SHA `0008d99873f815b23f0bea0c9fca989a20b0637e`, branch `foundation/domain-decoupled-core-v0`, explicit allowed/excluded paths, positive gates, planted negative controls, evidence lane, Shadow checkpoints and Human-owned operations.

Current local task-packet SHA-256 after Shadow reconciliation:
`e8362ae05d981a56cf597687f3d6193c2dd77a94d61ef6385c33c75afe29269c`

This digest is candidate evidence only and must be recomputed after any mutation.

## Shadow Architect FIRST_GREEN findings
Current outcome: `RECONCILE_BEFORE_NEXT_STEP_L2`.

Material gaps found and locally resolved:
1. **Missing real root atom** — the Epic was conceptual only; this issue now owns a disjoint Foundation lease.
2. **False dependency on future P2 contracts** — the first Foundation validator read `contracts/**` even though #3 owns those bytes. The gate is now self-contained using Foundation fixtures/task packet; P2 retains exclusive domain-contract ownership.
3. **False-green public boundary auditor** — exclusion matching used absolute path components, so a workspace under `/mnt/data` skipped the entire repository. It now evaluates repo-relative paths and has a regression test for `/mnt/data` workspaces.

Still open:
- the executable candidate bytes are local and are not yet the exact GitHub Foundation head;
- no commit/push/PR/merge authority is inferred from local gates;
- source/PDF truth, private resolver, domain contracts, native/device/runtime, model-quality and Human lanes remain separate downstream work.

## Local candidate evidence after reconciliation
Restored candidate positive gates:
- `PYTHONPATH=src python -m edge_tlm.cli validate` -> PASS (`foundation packet, DAG semantics, handoff cardinality, and required SSOT surfaces`)
- `PYTHONPATH=src python -m edge_tlm.cli audit-public-boundary` -> PASS
- `PYTHONPATH=src python -m pytest -q` -> **16 passed**

Executed planted controls:
- planted private Google Workspace URL -> boundary gate FAIL as required;
- second `ACTIVE` Local Handoff item -> validate FAIL as required;
- cyclic Foundation DAG -> validate FAIL as required;
- fixtures restored -> all positive gates green again.

These are `LOCAL_DETERMINISTIC` candidate receipts, not repository/device/Human acceptance.

## Required pre-implementation gates
- repository mission and provider-neutral invariants are explicit;
- State Machine, true-dependency DAG, request data flow, evidence lanes and molecular issue index are readable from root SSOT;
- Builder vs Shadow Architect ownership and L0-L3 checkpoints are explicit;
- task packet requires allowed/excluded paths, start/completion dependencies, positive gates, negative controls, evidence lane, rollback and Human-owned operations;
- Local Handoff contract keeps exactly one ACTIVE item and never implies execution;
- Foundation validation has zero dependency on future-owned `contracts/**`;
- no private Google Workspace URL/value, credential, roadmap or commercial text appears in public bytes.

## Acceptance gates on exact GitHub head
- rebind exact base and stage only the #15 publication manifest;
- `edge-tlmctl validate`;
- `edge-tlmctl audit-public-boundary`;
- `pytest -q`;
- rerun private-URL, multi-ACTIVE-handoff and cyclic-DAG canaries;
- GitHub changed-path readback confirms only #15 lease paths changed;
- Shadow `
